Z||000006||FieroJoe||11-02-2001||07:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierospeeder:<BR><B>im just concerned about the wiring, and the neutral start switch.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The main difference with wiring that I know about is with the backup lights.  You'll just need to rig up your own way to make them come on unless you can find the correct engine wiring harness that will have the connector on it.  Also, you will need the correct ECM for the engine and tranny that you are going to be using.  You will not have a neutral start switch, nor will you need to do any additional wiring because of it.  The neutral start switch is just in the car itself and with the steering column and all that, and you wont be removing any wiring that will prompt you to rewire how your starter gets power.<P>You will also have something that most (stock) manual tranny fiero owners envy; the stupid key retainer lever that you have to push to get your key out!<P><BR>||||reg||1
